Package: EpiExposure
Type: Package
Title: Epidemiological Framework for Interpreting Distributed Lag Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
	person("Ricardo", "Tomaz",
       	email = "ricardogomesagro@gmail.com",
       	role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description:
	Provides an epidemiological framework for structuring and interpreting
	exposure–lag–response associations fitted using distributed lag non-linear
	models (DLNMs). The package builds on the statistical infrastructure of the
	'dlnm' package by formalising epidemiological concepts such as exposure
	windows, biologically meaningful lag periods, and standardised cumulative
	summaries. EpiExposure does not redefine DLNM methodology, but supplies
	reproducible, domain-oriented workflows for epidemiological studies,
	particularly in climate–disease and plant disease epidemiology.
